    "created_at": "2018-11-29T12:52:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-11-29T12:52:52Z",
    "body": "> It seems that might end up being quite a bit of request bloat though, especially as we get more module types.\r\n\r\nThis did occur to me, especially when I refreshed myself on the list of accepted JavaScript MIME types (which was the reason I suggested the modern subset, e.g. dropping `javascript1.x`, `jscript` and friends) 😕 I guess it could get pretty large if a significant number of module types were added, though I don't know how much of a concern it would be.",
